        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    stock_price = 48.6\n    strike_price = 45\n    time_to_expiration = 0.25\n    risk_free_rate = 0.003\n    n_d1 = 0.6352\n    n_d2 = 0.5486\n\n    # Calculate the put value using the Black-Scholes formula\n    from math import exp\n\n    put_value = (\n        strike_price\n        * exp(-risk_free_rate * time_to_expiration)\n        * (1 - n_d2)\n        - stock_price * (1 - n_d1)\n    )\n\n    # return answer\n    return round(put_value, 3)\n```",
